# p_comm_s4: probe, measured on the whole-model graphs (s4_param_defer's configuration).
#
# question   s5_per_layer: host peak -24%, VRAM byte-identical, transcript 524,288 B and one round
#            below s4_param_defer (0.0047%); phase B requires identical bytes. Where is the round?
# excluded   mask sub-graph (traced literally): 0 bytes, 0 rounds; sub-graph sum equals the reported
#            transcript; per-layer impossible (would be a multiple of 12). Same difference between the
#            lever-free baselines (CPU 11,228,688,384/1495, GPU 11,229,212,672/1496).
# probe      graphop_comm_gpu reads CrypTen comm_bytes and comm_rounds before and after each graph node.
# order      instrument loaded last (param_defer_gpu rewrites Graph.forward; an earlier wrapper would
#            be lost silently).
# scope      probe only (two integer reads and one line per node; SHAFT_LEVERS in p_ steps).
SHAFT_LIMB_LOOP=1
SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16
SHAFT_LEVERS=param_spill_gpu,param_defer_gpu,graphop_comm_gpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_PARAM_SPILL=1 SNNI_SPILL_DIR=/results"
